  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CST THU NOV 26 2026\n\nA few light returns can be seen on the KBMX radar this evening.\nWith temperatures already in the mid 30s and falling, we would\nexpect to see a few locations see some snow flurries over the\nnext couple of hours. No accumulations are expected. Low temps\ntonight will hover around the freezing mark for most as lingering\ncloud cover as a breezy northwesterly wind hold temps a bit\nwarmer than guidance has been hinting at.\n\nRain-free conditions are in store for Friday and Saturday as\ndrier air works into the region. Clearing skies will allow for\ntemps to plummet into the mid 20s across the northern half of the\nCWA Saturday morning. We look to add on about 10 degrees on\nSaturday as southerly flow returns. This will also begin to usher\nGulf moisture back across the Southeast in advance of our next\nstorm system. By Sunday, an upper trough will dig across the\nPlains and lift across the Southeast. An associated cold front\nwill swing through the region Sunday afternoon through early\nMonday morning. We will continue with medium to high chances for\nrain Sunday into early Monday morning as this feature moves\nthrough. Thunderstorm chances will be low as instability is\nlimited. However, we can't rule out a rogue thunderstorm or two\nduring the day. Cooler and drier weather is expected early next\nweek as surface high pressure takes control.\n\n95/Castillo",
